From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tempeste <tempeste@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 16:48:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/33] flashnext: batched picks, riding prompt pieces, shared
 kept rows, expert lending, HC tiles

The prompt-cache mark off the critical path, one-launch draft and verify picks, a fix for rank 0's n-gram history
under PLE_PEER, last prompt pieces riding mixed rounds, exact sequence-parallel passes, pacing and packing of riding
pieces, a lane-host time ledger, decode GEMM and router tiles, the batched draft head split over both ranks, kept
states sharing their rows (pshare) with recurrent anchors, lending the light rank's copies of the peer's experts,
and HC read-out and output tile variants.

Changes, in the order they were made:
- perf(flashnext): take the prompt-cache mark off the critical path (four opt-in flags)
- perf(flashnext): pick a shared round's drafts in one launch (opt-in TF_FLASHNEXT_DRAFT_PICK_BATCH)
- fix(flashnext): keep rank 0's n-gram history moving when PLE_PEER skips its gather
- perf(flashnext): take a shared verify pass's candidates in one launch (opt-in TF_FLASHNEXT_VERIFY_PICK_BATCH)
- test(flashnext): judge PROMPT_MULTI at the window's 1,536-row cap
- flashnext: copy drawn candidates back in the batched verify pick
- flashnext: last pieces ride mixed rounds, packed prompts keep the in-pass mark
- flashnext: a mixed round's piece takes its alone pass's sums (TF_FLASHNEXT_MIXED_SEQPAR)
- flashnext: a mixed piece joins its open sums before the head, as chunk() does
- flashnext: remove start-of-pass idle on prompt passes behind three rank-local flags
- perf(flashnext): dtile prompt tiles behind TF_FLASHNEXT_PROMPT_DTILE (opt-in, same bits)
- flashnext: TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_SUM_OVERLAP hides a sub-1536-row prompt pass's rank sums behind its own rows
- flashnext: TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_SEQPAR_EXACT runs seqpar exactly on 512 to 1535-row prompt passes
- flashnext: TF_FLASHNEXT_HC_DECODE_SPLIT puts a decode pass's hyper-connection read-out on one row tile (same bytes)
- flashnext: report a prompt a riding last piece finished instead of re-opening its lane
- lane host: TF_FLASHNEXT_MIXED_PACE sizes riding pieces to the decode share
- prompt cache: TF_FLASHNEXT_PCACHE_EXPLAIN, _ONE_COPY and _VALUE (default off)
- flashnext: TF_FLASHNEXT_PREFILL_MANY=<spans> packs waiting whole prompts into one prompt pass under OVERLAP (needs
  PROMPT_MULTI; default off)
- lane host: TENSORFOLD_LANE_LEDGER_MS=<ms> logs where the engine thread's wall time went each period (rounds, rows
  that rode, prompt calls by kind, visits, switches, waiting; default off)
- flashnext: TF_FLASHNEXT_DECODE_GEMM and TF_FLASHNEXT_ROUTE_DECODE, decode-round GEMMs and router tiles with the same
  bytes (default off)
- flashnext: TF_FLASHNEXT_MIXED_RIDE_FAST=1 keeps a riding piece's split sums and exchanges on the sums stream
  (default off)
- flashnext: TF_FLASHNEXT_PCACHE_SHARE=1, kept states share their rows (default off)
- flashnext: TF_FLASHNEXT_PCACHE_ANCHOR_TOKENS=<n>, recurrent-state anchors at chunk ends and branch-point keeps
  (needs PCACHE_SHARE; default off)
- feat(flashnext): split the batched draft head's passes across both ranks
- flashnext: pshare keeps size a keep after its evictions, replay token bytes flag, flashnext-pshare GPU byte test
- flashnext: pshare anchors at riding and packed piece ends, the rows segment reserved early, chains capped by
  grafting
- flashnext: flashnext-pshare-ride GPU byte test, replay pieces, chain depth and the anchors-as-built arm
- flashnext: TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_ROUTE_BESIDE crosses a seqpar pass's mixed rows beside the router and runs the shared
  expert's own rows under the gather, flashnext-route-beside GPU byte test
- Lend the light rank's copies of the peer's experts behind TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_LEND
- Add TF_FLASHNEXT_OUT_TILE: 128 x 128 lane-order tiles for 64-row MXFP8 calls from 256 rows
- Add TF_FLASHNEXT_HCW: byte-identical read-out variants and the hcw / out-tile benches
- flashnext: a riding piece keeps its alone pass's warm, route-beside and a second stream for the windows' front
  (three default-off flags)
- Lend beside riding rows, a hot lent set from routing counts, and the routing count capture
- Add TF_FLASHNEXT_HCW wb= and dec=2: the write-back fused with the down, the decode up on persistent CTAs, and their
  hcw bench

Flags this patch adds (a flag's default is its unset value; unset leaves the engine as it was
before the flag, and a knob named under another flag only matters when that flag is on):
- TENSORFOLD_LANE_LEDGER_MS: unset and 0 are off, whole milliseconds up to ten minutes, anything else refused
- TF_FLASHNEXT_DECODE_GEMM: added by the change "TF_FLASHNEXT_DECODE_GEMM and TF_FLASHNEXT_ROUTE_DECODE, decode-round
  GEMMs and router tiles with the same bytes (default off)".
- TF_FLASHNEXT_DRAFT_KEEP=1 (--tp 2): the MTP head caches' device block and host rows are kept across requests instead
  of allocated at every open (same bytes); off unset or 0.
- TF_FLASHNEXT_DRAFT_PICK_BATCH=1 picks each draft head step's best and sampling candidates for all of the round's
  streams in one launch instead of one small launch a stream, with the same drafts and replies.
- TF_FLASHNEXT_GATHER_OPEN=1: the first prompt chunk's n-gram row gather starts when the request opens, before the
  head caches and the prompt-cache restore; off unset or 0.
- TF_FLASHNEXT_HCD_DN / TF_FLASHNEXT_HCD_UP (with TF_FLASHNEXT_HC_DECODE_SPLIT): the row tile of the decode read-out's
  down and up kernels; unset: chosen by the pass's rows.
- TF_FLASHNEXT_HCW is off unset or 0, takes each key once in range, picks by rows below lo, and leaves the identity
  bits alone
- TF_FLASHNEXT_HCW_UP_CTAS=N: the grid of the wide up+mix kernel in prompt passes (same bytes at any value); unset or
  0: the engine's grid.
- TF_FLASHNEXT_HC_DECODE_SPLIT: added by the change "TF_FLASHNEXT_HC_DECODE_SPLIT puts a decode pass's
  hyper-connection read-out on one row tile (same bytes)".
- TF_FLASHNEXT_MARK_IN_PASS=N (1 to 512) captures a mark at most N rows before a pass's end inside that pass instead
  of running the last rows as a pass of their own.
- TF_FLASHNEXT_MIXED_LAST (--tp 2 with TF_FLASHNEXT_OVERLAP, else refused at load) lets more pieces wait for the next
  decode round and ride it (one piece waits at a time; the lane host ends its visit once one waits).
- TF_FLASHNEXT_MIXED_PACE is off unset or 0, on at 1, refuses anything else, needs --tp 2 and TF_FLASHNEXT_OVERLAP,
  and leaves the identity alone
- TF_FLASHNEXT_MIXED_RIDE_BESIDE: the shared expert's two calls cover the piece's rows and the ride's, each a
  contiguous run, the first holding the own half
- TF_FLASHNEXT_MIXED_RIDE_FAST is off unset or 0, on at 1, refuses anything else, sets no tp_flags bit and needs
  TF_FLASHNEXT_MIXED_SEQPAR at --tp 2 with mixed rounds
- TF_FLASHNEXT_MIXED_RIDE_FRONT=1: a riding window's front launches its glue kernels and staged uploads on the side
  stream too; off unset or 0.
- TF_FLASHNEXT_MIXED_RIDE_WARM, _FRONT and _BESIDE are off unset or 0, on at 1, refuse anything else, set no tp_flags
  bit and need their companions
- TF_FLASHNEXT_MIXED_SEQPAR=1 (--tp 2 with mixed rounds, else refused at load): a mixed round's piece takes the sums
  its alone pass takes (TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_SPLIT_SUM's halves, TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_SEQPAR's row exchanges with
  TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_SCATTER_BF16, TF_FLASHNE...
- TF_FLASHNEXT_MTP_CACHE_ONLY=1 runs the MTP head's prompt rows of a non-final chunk only as far as its cache writes.
- TF_FLASHNEXT_OUT_TILE is off unset or 0, the 128 x 128 lane-order tile at 1 (16 warps) or 2 (8 warps), refuses
  anything else and leaves the identity bits alone
- TF_FLASHNEXT_PCACHE_ANCHOR_TOKENS: added by the change "TF_FLASHNEXT_PCACHE_ANCHOR_TOKENS=<n>, recurrent-state
  anchors at chunk ends and branch-point keeps (needs PCACHE_SHARE; default off)".
- TF_FLASHNEXT_PCACHE_EXPLAIN: added by the change "prompt cache: TF_FLASHNEXT_PCACHE_EXPLAIN, _ONE_COPY and _VALUE
  (default off)".
- TF_FLASHNEXT_PCACHE_ONE_COPY=1: a kept state that a longer state of the same request extends is evicted after
  superseded states and before any idle one; off unset or 0.
- TF_FLASHNEXT_PCACHE_SHARE: added by the change "TF_FLASHNEXT_PCACHE_SHARE=1, kept states share their rows (default
  off)".
- TF_FLASHNEXT_PCACHE_VALUE=1: idle kept states are evicted in greedy-dual-size order instead of least recently used;
  off unset or 0.
- TF_FLASHNEXT_PREFILL_MANY is off unset or 0, takes 2 to 16 spans, refuses anything else, needs PROMPT_MULTI and
  OVERLAP, and leaves the identity alone
- TF_FLASHNEXT_PROMPT_DTILE: added by the change "dtile prompt tiles behind TF_FLASHNEXT_PROMPT_DTILE (opt-in, same
  bits)".
- TF_FLASHNEXT_RESTORE_ASYNC=1: no host wait after a prompt-cache restore's copies (later work is ordered on the same
  stream); off unset or 0.
- TF_FLASHNEXT_ROUTE_DECODE: added by the change "TF_FLASHNEXT_DECODE_GEMM and TF_FLASHNEXT_ROUTE_DECODE, decode-round
  GEMMs and router tiles with the same bytes (default off)".
- TF_FLASHNEXT_SNAP_EARLY=1 allocates the kept state's buffer while the marked pass still runs (both ranks at --tp 2).
- TF_FLASHNEXT_SNAP_SPLIT=1 copies the model's part of the state while the head still runs.
- TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_DRAFT_SPLIT is off unset or 0, on at 1, refuses anything else and sets identity bit 34 alone
- TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_LEND is off unset or 0, takes 8 to 128 experts in powers of two, refuses anything else and sets bits
  36 to 42 with its row floor
- TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_LEND_COUNT=<path> (with TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_LEND): writes the routing counts of passes of 512 rows or
  more, every 8 passes, for TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_LEND_SET; unset: no file.
- TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_LEND_MIN_ROWS=<rows> (with TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_LEND): the fewest rows of a pass that lends experts.
- TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_LEND_RIDE and TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_LEND_SET set bits 43 and 44 with lending alone,
  TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_LEND_COUNT none, and bad values or either without lending refuse the load
- TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_LEND_SET=<counts file> (with TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_LEND): lends each layer's busiest experts from a
  routing-counts file; unset: the default lent set.
- TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_ROUTE_BESIDE is off unset or 0, on at 1, refuses anything else and sets identity bit 15 alone
- TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_SEQPAR_EXACT is off unset or 0, on at 1, refuses anything else, lowers the seqpar and split floors
  to 512 rows unless TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_SEQPAR_MIN_ROWS names one, and sets identity bit 33
- TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_SUM_OVERLAP is off unset or 0, on at 1, refuses anything else, lowers the split floor to 512 rows
  but not seqpar's, and sets identity bit 32
- TF_FLASHNEXT_VERIFY_PICK_BATCH=1 (with TF_FLASHNEXT_SAMPLE_CAND=1) takes the sampled windows' candidates from one
  launch over the pass's own score rows instead of one launch a window, with the same draws and replies.
